{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q8ECH6","uniProtkbId":"HEPT_SHEON","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2021-04-07","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-11-04","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2003-03-01","entryVersion":102,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Shewanella oneidensis (strain ATCC 700550 / JCM 31522 / CIP 106686 / LMG 19005 / NCIMB 14063 / MR-1)","taxonId":211586,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Gammaproteobacteria","Alteromonadales","Shewanellaceae","Shewanella"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"mRNA nuclease HepT"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29555683"}],"value":"3.1.-.-"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"value":"Toxin HepT"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"value":"hepT"},"orderedLocusNames":[{"value":"SO_3166"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26112399"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29555683"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"value":"Toxic component of a type VII toxin-antitoxin (TA) system. A bacteriostatic toxin; upon overexpression in situ or in E.coli inhibits cell growth. Cells swell slightly. Neutralized by cognate antitoxin MntA (PubMed:26112399, PubMed:29555683, PubMed:33045733). Cleaves mRNA in a probably endonucleolytic manner; has no activity on rRNA, tRNA, ssDNA or dsDNA. The TA system confers plasmid stability in E.coli (PubMed:29555683). Neutralization is mostly due to tri-AMPylation by MntA (PubMed:33045733)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26112399"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29555683"}],"value":"Forms a complex with cognate antitoxin MntA (PubMed:26112399). Forms a heterooctamer with cognate antitoxin MntA with stoichiometry HepT(6):MntA(2). Two HepT molecules dimerize to form a cleft with 2 Rx4-6H active site motifs in close proximity that probably bind substrate; in the heterooctamer 3 HepT dimers form (PubMed:29555683)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26112399"}],"value":"Expressed during exponential growth, part of the mntA-hepT operon. Under control of MntA"}],"commentType":"INDUCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"value":"Tri-AMPylated by cognate antitoxin MntA on Tyr-104; this rotates the residue nearly 180 degrees. Modified protein has much less RNase activity"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"commentType":"MASS SPECTROMETRY","method":"Electrospray","molWeight":16191.46,"molWeightError":0.0,"note":"6-His tagged, no AMPylation, probably in situ.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}]},{"commentType":"MASS SPECTROMETRY","method":"Electrospray","molWeight":17122.06,"molWeightError":0.0,"note":"6-His tagged, modified by 3 AMP, probably in situ.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26112399"}],"value":"When mntA-hepT is deleted, has a sight reduction in swimming motility. No effect when just this gene is deleted"}],"commentType":"DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the HepT RNase toxin family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":133,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"mRNA nuclease HepT","featureId":"PRO_0000452433"},{"type":"Motif","location":{"start":{"value":97,"modifier":"EXA